      "official_mark_scheme_text": "$\\pi\\int_1^{3/2}\\frac{16}{(2x-1)^4}dx=\\pi\\left(-\\frac{16}{3\\times2(2x-1)^3}\\right)$. *M1 — integrate $y^2$; M0 for more than one error. Antiderivative as shown. A1. Substitute limits: $\\pi(-16/(6\\times8)+16/(6\\times1))=\\frac{7\\pi}{3}$. DM1 — correct limits, at least $(-1/3+8/3)$; allow one sign error. Cylinder volume $\\pi\\times1^2\\times\\frac12=\\frac\\pi2$. B1. Volume $\\frac{7\\pi}{3}-\\frac\\pi2=\\frac{11\\pi}{6}$. A1; A0 for 5.76 not exact; SC B1 for $11\\pi/6$ if DM0 for insufficient substitution or B0. Total 5.",
